Aerie-Purpose: Register the Tab Model prefs (archive and sleep delays) and let the settings page read and write them.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/prefs (browser_prefs.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #176. The prefs are aerie.tabs.archive_after (a string: 12h, 24h, 7d or never) and
aerie.tabs.sleep_after_minutes (a number: 0 for never, else 15 to 480). Their names,
defaults and parsing are in components/aerie_tab_model (tab_model_prefs.*). The favourites
cap is a constant there, not a pref. The names are string literals in the settings_private
allowlist, as for the other Aerie prefs, and a test compares them with the constants.
Nothing reads the prefs yet but the Tab Model service; the settings controls come with the
slices that own the archive and sleep behaviour.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
@@ -485,4 +485,10 @@
   // The name is aerie_fonts::kRestrictFonts; a test compares the two.
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.fonts.restrict"] = settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
+  // Aerie: when Today tabs are archived, and when idle tabs sleep (issue #176).
+  // The names are aerie_tab_model::kArchiveAfter and kSleepAfterMinutes; a test
+  // compares them.
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.archive_after"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.sleep_after_minutes"] =
+      settings_api::PrefType::kNumber;
 
   // Privacy page
